<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Pablo Pérez Alfonzo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Pablo Pérez Alfonzo was a Venezuelan lawyer and Democratic Action politician who, as minister of development and later of mines and hydrocarbons, shaped the country's oil policy. He helped introduce the fifty-fifty profit-sharing principle in 1948 and in 1960 was a principal founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opec">OPEC</a>, together with Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>'s Abdullah Tariki. Late in life he warned of oil's damaging effects, calling it 'the devil's excrement'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-pablo-perez-alfonzo.jpg" alt="Juan Pablo Pérez Alfonzo" width="320" height="579" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This work was first published in Venezuela and is now in the public domain becau... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Pablo_P%C3%A9rez_Alfonzo_(1964).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
